> Time: 1439257310 / Tue, 11 Aug 2015 01:41:50 +0000
> URL: /index.php?/REST/Forums/topic/getPosts?topicId=79237&SessionId=ea165abc6d8fee8fd6620efe9caf5442
> User dl0478 (284081)
Request Time: 0 seconds
{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"199.168.151.142","IsFirstPost":true,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79237,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"2ef8688f2bd206583f51a50f674204ff","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Hi all,&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I&#039;m newly engaged (well about a month old - April 30th). My guy proposed to me on the beach at Now Larimar in Punta Cana the day after close friends of ours married. It was amazing and I was totally surprised, no idea it was happening at all!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Anyways, we are doing destination wedding, all inclusive somewhere in Mexico. Haven&#039;t narrowed down what resort exactly yet, but looking for May 2016, family-friendly, not in the heart of the hotel zone in Cancun (we want a more resort feel rather than a bunch of high rises right next to each other), great beach for pictures of course and our ceremony location (possibly reception location), has to have night time entertainment\/disco for dancing, we would prefer no reservations for the a la carte restaurants (we were spoiled at Now), and no wrist bands if possible = Dreams resorts seems to be the only one I know of that has the last 2 features. Are there any others? I&#039;m sure there are a ton of other things I&#039;m forgetting about our wants, and I also find myself thinking a lot about my guests and their wants\/needs before my own vision, so I think this is why I&#039;m having a super difficult time choosing a resort that hopefully has the date I am shooting for. Has anyone else had this issue? Also, reading both positiv and negative reviews for resorts, as well as previous brides&#039; experiences are making it very difficult for me to choose a resort, as well. I&#039;m worried I am going to pick a bad one or have an awful experience. I have been in contact with a TA from apple vacations and Beach Bums vacations, both of which have only responded to my inquiries a few times and I feel like time is a ticking and I need to get these save the dates out like yesterday for guests to start budgeting for their vacation next year.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Any thoughts\/suggestions\/concerns greatly appreciated.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1897673,"PostDate":1433171123,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Hi all,<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I'm newly engaged (well about a month old - April 30th). My guy proposed to me on the beach at Now Larimar in Punta Cana the day after close friends of ours married. It was amazing and I was totally surprised, no idea it was happening at all!<\/p>\n<p>Anyways, we are doing destination wedding, all inclusive somewhere in Mexico. Haven't narrowed down what resort exactly yet, but looking for May 2016, family-friendly, not in the heart of the hotel zone in Cancun (we want a more resort feel rather than a bunch of high rises right next to each other), great beach for pictures of course and our ceremony location (possibly reception location), has to have night time entertainment\/disco for dancing, we would prefer no reservations for the a la carte restaurants (we were spoiled at Now), and no wrist bands if possible = Dreams resorts seems to be the only one I know of that has the last 2 features. Are there any others? I'm sure there are a ton of other things I'm forgetting about our wants, and I also find myself thinking a lot about my guests and their wants\/needs before my own vision, so I think this is why I'm having a super difficult time choosing a resort that hopefully has the date I am shooting for. Has anyone else had this issue? Also, reading both positiv and negative reviews for resorts, as well as previous brides' experiences are making it very difficult for me to choose a resort, as well. I'm worried I am going to pick a bad one or have an awful experience. I have been in contact with a TA from apple vacations and Beach Bums vacations, both of which have only responded to my inquiries a few times and I feel like time is a ticking and I need to get these save the dates out like yesterday for guests to start budgeting for their vacation next year.<\/p>\n<p>Any thoughts\/suggestions\/concerns greatly appreciated.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"ashlynm_88@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"199.168.151.142","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1433169080,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-283337.jpg?_r=1435688507","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":212,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"ashlynm88","Id":283337,"Name":"ashlynm88","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"24.85.127.174","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79237,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"67d91c2365c38498f4f998c18082620f","RawContent":"I think the general consensus is that picking the resort is one of the toughest parts of planning a DW. There are lots of good suggestions here on how to do your research and then narrow it down. I looked at and compared both wedding packages and the actual resort amenities\/costs for guests. I also worked with a TA to get prices for resorts. And read lots of trip advisor reviews. Good luck!\n\n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk","Attachments":[],"Id":1897711,"PostDate":1433237038,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                I think the general consensus is that picking the resort is one of the toughest parts of planning a DW. There are lots of good suggestions here on how to do your research and then narrow it down. I looked at and compared both wedding packages and the actual resort amenities\/costs for guests. I also worked with a TA to get prices for resorts. And read lots of trip advisor reviews. Good luck!<br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>- Erin<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My planning thread:\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79068-vancouverpetunia-now-sapphire-april-7-2016\/?p=1893268'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79068-vancouverpetunia-now-sapphire-april-7-2016\/?p=1893268<\/a>","Email":"ekjzwedding@gmail.com","IpAddress":"24.85.127.174","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1417435045,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281283.jpg?_r=1428779369","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"vancouverpetunia","Id":281283,"Name":"vancouverpetunia","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"71.41.201.34","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79237,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"33496ede4e0ca8523df53e19799ec74c","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"ashlynm88\"] Choosing the resort was the most difficult and frustrating part for me! I wanted everything to be perfect for our guests and family friendly. I think I read every trip advisor review for ever resort in Mexico. One thing I had to remember is that even the perfect resort will have a few bad reviews - someone there will have a bad experience. If you look up your favorite restaurant, you&#039;ll probably see a few bad reviews.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Have you looked at Moon Palace? I&#039;m getting married at Beach Palace, but we stayed at Moon Palace in December and it definitely has a resort feel. It is huge with tons of amenities for families and adults (golf course, dolphin swim, putt putt golf, a kids zone fun room, a teen room, etc.). &amp;nbsp;It also has a disco for nightlife. &amp;nbsp;The food there was great! You do have to wear a wristband at Moon Palace, but I think that is the case for most all inclusives. I&#039;ve been told the wedding party can cut the wristband off for the wedding and you can get a new one (but maybe check on that before you book...). &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1897725,"PostDate":1433243059,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"283337\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/283337-ashlynm88\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">ashlynm88<\/span><\/a> Choosing the resort was the most difficult and frustrating part for me! I wanted everything to be perfect for our guests and family friendly. I think I read every trip advisor review for ever resort in Mexico. One thing I had to remember is that even the perfect resort will have a few bad reviews - someone there will have a bad experience. If you look up your favorite restaurant, you'll probably see a few bad reviews.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Have you looked at Moon Palace? I'm getting married at Beach Palace, but we stayed at Moon Palace in December and it definitely has a resort feel. It is huge with tons of amenities for families and adults (golf course, dolphin swim, putt putt golf, a kids zone fun room, a teen room, etc.). \u00a0It also has a disco for nightlife. \u00a0The food there was great! You do have to wear a wristband at Moon Palace, but I think that is the case for most all inclusives. I've been told the wedding party can cut the wristband off for the wedding and you can get a new one (but maybe check on that before you book...). \u00a0<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"erikahime@gmail.com","IpAddress":"208.191.153.24","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1421803507,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281815.jpg?_r=1431031761","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":278,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Danielle1","Id":281815,"Name":"Danielle1","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"142.56.86.35","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79237,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"24f358ba60fd7e4d7cc4a879e1a8a44e","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"ashlynm88\"]&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Dreams, Secrets, Now, Breathless (It&#039;s a whole chain that has what you are looking for in terms of no reservations and no wrist bands). So far the resorts of theirs I&#039;ve stayed at are amazing and I will pretty much always want to stay at them. They are higher end and just generally beautiful. The Secrets chain is adults only which is pretty nice. We had really tried to get something in the AM Resort chain (this chain) but it was just too expensive for our guests to fly out. If you are doing a small wedding I would highly recommend it. If you are trying to cut costs or have a tight butdet I wouldn&#039;t go with the AM Resorts unless you get a killer deal.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We are getting married at the Grand Serenis in the Mayan Riviera. Looks beautiful and looks like its not crowded by other resorts close by. They have a private beach and palapa for weddings you can book which is what sold the resort for us. We wanted to keep things private from other guests so no one was staring at us or watching our wedding while in their swim suits drinking tequilla haha.&amp;nbsp; Check out @[member=\"calgarybride2015\"]&#039;s review and planning thread. It seems amazing.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I would also recommend Cabo. Its got more of a traditional Mexico feel to it. We tried to get married there but nothing came back in our price range :( Good luck!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1897733,"PostDate":1433244358,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"283337\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/283337-ashlynm88\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">ashlynm88<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n<p>Dreams, Secrets, Now, Breathless (It's a whole chain that has what you are looking for in terms of no reservations and no wrist bands). So far the resorts of theirs I've stayed at are amazing and I will pretty much always want to stay at them. They are higher end and just generally beautiful. The Secrets chain is adults only which is pretty nice. We had really tried to get something in the AM Resort chain (this chain) but it was just too expensive for our guests to fly out. If you are doing a small wedding I would highly recommend it. If you are trying to cut costs or have a tight butdet I wouldn't go with the AM Resorts unless you get a killer deal.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We are getting married at the Grand Serenis in the Mayan Riviera. Looks beautiful and looks like its not crowded by other resorts close by. They have a private beach and palapa for weddings you can book which is what sold the resort for us. We wanted to keep things private from other guests so no one was staring at us or watching our wedding while in their swim suits drinking tequilla haha.\u00a0 Check out @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"277873\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/277873-calgarybride2015\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">calgarybride2015<\/span><\/a>'s review and planning thread. It seems amazing.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I would also recommend Cabo. Its got more of a traditional Mexico feel to it. We tried to get married there but nothing came back in our price range <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/sad.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':(' \/> Good luck!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>~*~YYCBRIDE2016~*~<\/p><p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79227-yycbride2016-grand-sirenis-planning-thread-february-2016\/'>My planning thread\u00a0<\/a><\/p><p>\u00a0<\/p><p><a class='bbc_url' href='http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/'><br><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10730;484\/st\/20160223\/e\/Our+Wedding\/dt\/-1\/k\/4bd8\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><br><\/a><br>\u00a0","Email":"janellepaquin@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"162.157.216.37","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1432086904,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-283167.jpg?_r=1432133572","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":133,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"yycbride2016","Id":283167,"Name":"yycbride2016","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"200.79.251.123","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79237,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"1e10056f4b6bb17d4a3787932fc2c67a","RawContent":"[quote name=\"ashlynm88\" post=\"1897673\" timestamp=\"1433185523\"]\nHi all,\n\nI&#039;m newly engaged (well about a month old - April 30th). My guy proposed to me on the beach at Now Larimar in Punta Cana the day after close friends of ours married. It was amazing and I was totally surprised, no idea it was happening at all!\nAnyways, we are doing destination wedding, all inclusive somewhere in Mexico. Haven&#039;t narrowed down what resort exactly yet, but looking for May 2016, family-friendly, not in the heart of the hotel zone in Cancun (we want a more resort feel rather than a bunch of high rises right next to each other), great beach for pictures of course and our ceremony location (possibly reception location), has to have night time entertainment\/disco for dancing, we would prefer no reservations for the a la carte restaurants (we were spoiled at Now), and no wrist bands if possible = Dreams resorts seems to be the only one I know of that has the last 2 features. Are there any others? I&#039;m sure there are a ton of other things I&#039;m forgetting about our wants, and I also find myself thinking a lot about my guests and their wants\/needs before my own vision, so I think this is why I&#039;m having a super difficult time choosing a resort that hopefully has the date I am shooting for. Has anyone else had this issue? Also, reading both positiv and negative reviews for resorts, as well as previous brides&#039; experiences are making it very difficult for me to choose a resort, as well. I&#039;m worried I am going to pick a bad one or have an awful experience. I have been in contact with a TA from apple vacations and Beach Bums vacations, both of which have only responded to my inquiries a few times and I feel like time is a ticking and I need to get these save the dates out like yesterday for guests to start budgeting for their vacation next year.\nAny thoughts\/suggestions\/concerns greatly appreciated.[\/quote]Hey Ashlynm88,\n\nCongrats on your engagement and welcome to the forum.   Did you know the owners of this page are travel agent?  I would get in touch with them.  also its a good thing you have a list of things you want from the hotel.  \n\nMay is still a good month to get married here!\n\nHappy Planning!","Attachments":[],"Id":1897743,"PostDate":1433248444,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>ashlynm88, on 01 June 2015 - 03:05 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>Hi all,<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I'm newly engaged (well about a month old - April 30th). My guy proposed to me on the beach at Now Larimar in Punta Cana the day after close friends of ours married. It was amazing and I was totally surprised, no idea it was happening at all!<\/p>\n<p>Anyways, we are doing destination wedding, all inclusive somewhere in Mexico. Haven't narrowed down what resort exactly yet, but looking for May 2016, family-friendly, not in the heart of the hotel zone in Cancun (we want a more resort feel rather than a bunch of high rises right next to each other), great beach for pictures of course and our ceremony location (possibly reception location), has to have night time entertainment\/disco for dancing, we would prefer no reservations for the a la carte restaurants (we were spoiled at Now), and no wrist bands if possible = Dreams resorts seems to be the only one I know of that has the last 2 features. Are there any others? I'm sure there are a ton of other things I'm forgetting about our wants, and I also find myself thinking a lot about my guests and their wants\/needs before my own vision, so I think this is why I'm having a super difficult time choosing a resort that hopefully has the date I am shooting for. Has anyone else had this issue? Also, reading both positiv and negative reviews for resorts, as well as previous brides' experiences are making it very difficult for me to choose a resort, as well. I'm worried I am going to pick a bad one or have an awful experience. I have been in contact with a TA from apple vacations and Beach Bums vacations, both of which have only responded to my inquiries a few times and I feel like time is a ticking and I need to get these save the dates out like yesterday for guests to start budgeting for their vacation next year.<\/p>\n<p>Any thoughts\/suggestions\/concerns greatly appreciated.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>Hey Ashlynm88,<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Congrats on your engagement and welcome to the forum. \u00a0 Did you know the owners of this page are travel agent? \u00a0I would get in touch with them. \u00a0also its a good thing you have a list of things you want from the hotel. \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>May is still a good month to get married here!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Happy Planning!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>Dream Weddings Riviera Maya- We pay attention to your wishes and coordinate closely with you to ensure your wedding or event is planned to perfection!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color:rgb(40,40,40);\"><span style=\"font-family:arial;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">Dream Weddings Riviera Maya<\/span><\/span><\/span><br><span style=\"font-family:arial;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">weddingsinplayadelcarmen@gmail.com<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.dreamweddingsrivieramaya.com\/Home_Page.html'>http:\/\/www.dreamweddingsrivieramaya.com\/Home_Page.html<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color:rgb(40,40,40);\"><span style=\"font-family:arial;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">Happy Planning!<\/span><\/span><\/span><br><span style=\"color:rgb(40,40,40);\"><span style=\"font-family:arial;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">Joyce<\/span><\/span><\/span><br>\n\u00a0","Email":"weddingsinplayadelcarmen@gmail.com","IpAddress":"187.252.44.28","GroupId":49,"GroupName":"Insiders","JoinDate":1326839987,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-250090.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"dreamweddings","Id":250090,"Name":"dreamweddings","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"24.114.24.238","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79237,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"ee9da7c50648088a08a47a6bed2f78e9","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Congrats on your recent engagement ashlynm88 and welcome to our forum community!!! you&#039;ll find lots of great info, advice, ideas and support here to help with your planning decisions, as you can already see :)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Here are a few images of magical wedding \"moments that matter\" Linc captured at some recent NOW weddings in our gorgeous Mayan Riviera.....enjoy :)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;....from the &lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/media\/set\/?set=a.10152879942949487.1073741913.18683524486&amp;amp;type=3&#039;&gt;NOW Jade Wedding Album: &lt;\/a&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=\"https:\/\/scontent-sea1-1.xx.fbcdn.net\/hphotos-xap1\/t31.0-8\/10828083_10152879945629487_385058951217096100_o.jpg\" alt=\"10828083_10152879945629487_3850589512170\"&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=\"https:\/\/scontent-sea1-1.xx.fbcdn.net\/hphotos-xfa1\/t31.0-8\/10481829_10152879945984487_3218129313193200416_o.jpg\" alt=\"10481829_10152879945984487_3218129313193\"&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=\"https:\/\/scontent-sea1-1.xx.fbcdn.net\/hphotos-xpa1\/t31.0-8\/10454974_10152879946864487_8706743019344647108_o.jpg\" alt=\"10454974_10152879946864487_8706743019344\"&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;....or these from the &lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/media\/set\/?set=a.10152285887359487.1073741881.18683524486&amp;amp;type=3&#039;&gt;NOW Sapphire Wedding Album: &lt;\/a&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=\"https:\/\/scontent-sea1-1.xx.fbcdn.net\/hphotos-xfp1\/t31.0-8\/10012197_10152285889364487_524506458_o.jpg\" alt=\"10012197_10152285889364487_524506458_o.j\"&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=\"https:\/\/scontent-sea1-1.xx.fbcdn.net\/hphotos-xfp1\/t31.0-8\/10010300_10152285889709487_764706269_o.jpg\" alt=\"10010300_10152285889709487_764706269_o.j\"&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=\"https:\/\/scontent-sea1-1.xx.fbcdn.net\/hphotos-xfp1\/t31.0-8\/1909431_10152285892349487_154319466_o.jpg\" alt=\"1909431_10152285892349487_154319466_o.jp\"&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Wishing you happy research, and all the best with your plans - cheers!!! team MTM :)&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1897745,"PostDate":1433249025,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Congrats on your recent engagement ashlynm88 and welcome to our forum community!!! you'll find lots of great info, advice, ideas and support here to help with your planning decisions, as you can already see <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Here are a few images of magical wedding \"moments that matter\" Linc captured at some recent NOW weddings in our gorgeous Mayan Riviera.....enjoy <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>....from the <a href='https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/media\/set\/?set=a.10152879942949487.1073741913.18683524486&type=3' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>NOW Jade Wedding Album: <\/a><\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"https:\/\/scontent-sea1-1.xx.fbcdn.net\/hphotos-xap1\/t31.0-8\/10828083_10152879945629487_385058951217096100_o.jpg\" alt=\"10828083_10152879945629487_3850589512170\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"https:\/\/scontent-sea1-1.xx.fbcdn.net\/hphotos-xfa1\/t31.0-8\/10481829_10152879945984487_3218129313193200416_o.jpg\" alt=\"10481829_10152879945984487_3218129313193\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"https:\/\/scontent-sea1-1.xx.fbcdn.net\/hphotos-xpa1\/t31.0-8\/10454974_10152879946864487_8706743019344647108_o.jpg\" alt=\"10454974_10152879946864487_8706743019344\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>....or these from the <a href='https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/media\/set\/?set=a.10152285887359487.1073741881.18683524486&type=3' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>NOW Sapphire Wedding Album: <\/a><\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"https:\/\/scontent-sea1-1.xx.fbcdn.net\/hphotos-xfp1\/t31.0-8\/10012197_10152285889364487_524506458_o.jpg\" alt=\"10012197_10152285889364487_524506458_o.j\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"https:\/\/scontent-sea1-1.xx.fbcdn.net\/hphotos-xfp1\/t31.0-8\/10010300_10152285889709487_764706269_o.jpg\" alt=\"10010300_10152285889709487_764706269_o.j\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"https:\/\/scontent-sea1-1.xx.fbcdn.net\/hphotos-xfp1\/t31.0-8\/1909431_10152285892349487_154319466_o.jpg\" alt=\"1909431_10152285892349487_154319466_o.jp\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wishing you happy research, and all the best with your plans - cheers!!! team MTM <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p><img src=\"http:\/\/i711.photobucket.com\/albums\/ww116\/momentsthatmatter\/MTMLogo08-1.png\" alt=\"MTMLogo08-1.png\"><\/p>\n<p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.momentsthatmatterphotography.com'><strong><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">Moments That Matter Photography Studios, Playa del Carmen, Mexico<\/span><\/strong><\/a><\/p>\n<p>Canadian Award Winning Photojournalist serving Mayan Riviera<br>\nEmail: <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='mailto:contact@momentsthatmatterphotography.com'>contact@momentsthatmatterphotography.com<\/a><\/p>\n<p>Scoop on what we do:\u00a0 <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/reviews\/r\/4212-beautiful-november-wedding\/#review'>MTM Reviews<\/a><\/p>\n<p>Meet Lincoln & Team MTM: <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/vimeo.com\/51032621'>\"Meet Lincoln\" Video + see his Passion!!!<\/a>","Email":"momentsthatmatterphotography@gmail.com","IpAddress":"189.221.252.187","GroupId":49,"GroupName":"Insiders","JoinDate":1280196260,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-230711.png?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Moments That Matter","Id":230711,"Name":"Moments That Matter","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"199.168.151.142","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79237,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"7abf81e30efcc2b7b5fb86799e7e457c","RawContent":"[quote name=\"yycbride2016\" post=\"1897733\" timestamp=\"1433258758\"]\n@[member=\"ashlynm88\"]\nDreams, Secrets, Now, Breathless (It&#039;s a whole chain that has what you are looking for in terms of no reservations and no wrist bands). So far the resorts of theirs I&#039;ve stayed at are amazing and I will pretty much always want to stay at them. They are higher end and just generally beautiful. The Secrets chain is adults only which is pretty nice. We had really tried to get something in the AM Resort chain (this chain) but it was just too expensive for our guests to fly out. If you are doing a small wedding I would highly recommend it. If you are trying to cut costs or have a tight butdet I wouldn&#039;t go with the AM Resorts unless you get a killer deal.\n\nWe are getting married at the Grand Serenis in the Mayan Riviera. Looks beautiful and looks like its not crowded by other resorts close by. They have a private beach and palapa for weddings you can book which is what sold the resort for us. We wanted to keep things private from other guests so no one was staring at us or watching our wedding while in their swim suits drinking tequilla haha.  Check out @[member=\"calgarybride2015\"]&#039;s review and planning thread. It seems amazing.\n\nI would also recommend Cabo. Its got more of a traditional Mexico feel to it. We tried to get married there but nothing came back in our price range :( Good luck![\/quote]We just got back from a wedding at Now Larimar in Punta Cana (which is also where I got engaged :) and would probably look into those more if we didn&#039;t want to try and get a different feel from a resort (not the same restaurants)...but the Dreams resorts seemed easy and maybe that is just because those are the ones that had been recommended to me at first. We are probably looking at around 60-80 guests (maybe, that&#039;s just a guess right now).\nFor some reason I thought Moon Palace may be more out of the price range I was shooting for for my guests, but TA Wendy suggested that one as a possibility as well, so I may have to look further into that one. I&#039;m just concerned with it&#039;s size.\nI&#039;m really wanting a great beach (not too rocky, or at least has a walkable\/swimable area) and I keep reading mix reviews on the \"types\" of beaches in the different resort locations.\nI spent all night last night reading all of @[member=\"calgarybride2015\"] posts\/boards. She did an amazing job! And I really liked how she was able to do the \"free\" package and add on the upgrades and have the private dinner in the palapa. I did read that there are no \"free\" safes in the rooms, which I find very odd. Any info on that? I am definitely going to spend some more time researching Grand Sirenis this evening. I did see it was kind of far from the airport as well like Dreams Tulum, but I also think I should try and concentrate more on what I am looking for in location and the wedding all while making sure I keep their travel in budget too no matter the trip to and from the airport. That is just one of the things that I have had in the back of my mind the last few days in researching.\nThanks for you input! It is greatly appreciated!","Attachments":[],"Id":1897752,"PostDate":1433254830,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>yycbride2016, on 02 June 2015 - 11:25 AM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"283337\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/283337-ashlynm88\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">ashlynm88<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n<p>Dreams, Secrets, Now, Breathless (It's a whole chain that has what you are looking for in terms of no reservations and no wrist bands). So far the resorts of theirs I've stayed at are amazing and I will pretty much always want to stay at them. They are higher end and just generally beautiful. The Secrets chain is adults only which is pretty nice. We had really tried to get something in the AM Resort chain (this chain) but it was just too expensive for our guests to fly out. If you are doing a small wedding I would highly recommend it. If you are trying to cut costs or have a tight butdet I wouldn't go with the AM Resorts unless you get a killer deal.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We are getting married at the Grand Serenis in the Mayan Riviera. Looks beautiful and looks like its not crowded by other resorts close by. They have a private beach and palapa for weddings you can book which is what sold the resort for us. We wanted to keep things private from other guests so no one was staring at us or watching our wedding while in their swim suits drinking tequilla haha.\u00a0 Check out @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"277873\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/277873-calgarybride2015\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">calgarybride2015<\/span><\/a>'s review and planning thread. It seems amazing.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I would also recommend Cabo. Its got more of a traditional Mexico feel to it. We tried to get married there but nothing came back in our price range <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/sad.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':(' \/> Good luck!<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>We just got back from a wedding at Now Larimar in Punta Cana (which is also where I got engaged <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> and would probably look into those more if we didn't want to try and get a different feel from a resort (not the same restaurants)...but the Dreams resorts seemed easy and maybe that is just because those are the ones that had been recommended to me at first. We are probably looking at around 60-80 guests (maybe, that's just a guess right now).<\/p>\n<p>For some reason I thought Moon Palace may be more out of the price range I was shooting for\u00a0for my guests, but TA Wendy suggested that one as a possibility as well, so I may have to look further into that one. I'm just concerned with\u00a0it's size.<\/p>\n<p>I'm really wanting a great beach (not too rocky, or at least has a walkable\/swimable area) and I keep reading mix reviews on the \"types\" of beaches in the different resort locations.<\/p>\n<p>I spent all night last night reading all of @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"277873\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/277873-calgarybride2015\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">calgarybride2015<\/span><\/a> posts\/boards. She did an amazing job! And I really liked how she was able to do the \"free\" package and add on the upgrades and have the private dinner in the palapa. I did read that there are no \"free\" safes in the rooms, which I find very odd. Any info on that? I am definitely going to spend some more time researching Grand Sirenis this evening. I did see it was kind of far from the airport as well like Dreams Tulum, but I also think I should try and concentrate more on what I am looking for in location and the wedding all while making sure I keep their travel in budget too no matter the trip to and from the airport. That is just one of the things that I have had in the back of my mind the last few days in researching.<\/p>\n<p>Thanks for you input! It is greatly appreciated!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"ashlynm_88@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"199.168.151.142","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1433169080,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-283337.jpg?_r=1435688507","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":212,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"ashlynm88","Id":283337,"Name":"ashlynm88","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"100.33.96.77","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79237,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"8d3f3e6ad9c3754e9bde159f815c0deb","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Hi all,&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I&#039;m brand new to this forum and have looked at (what feels like) hundreds of resorts in Mexico and Dominican Republic. I was wondering if anyone has any suggestions for a budget friendly resort that has great food and a more modern feel. Hoping to have an April 2016 wedding date, thus... I need to get a move on it!&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Thank You!!!&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;- Regina&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1897942,"PostDate":1433456358,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Hi all,<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I'm brand new to this forum and have looked at (what feels like) hundreds of resorts in Mexico and Dominican Republic. I was wondering if anyone has any suggestions for a budget friendly resort that has great food and a more modern feel. Hoping to have an April 2016 wedding date, thus... I need to get a move on it!\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Thank You!!!\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>- Regina<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"reginakrachak@gmail.com","IpAddress":"100.33.96.77","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1433455831,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-283386.jpg?_r=1433470594","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":201,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"ReginaKay","Id":283386,"Name":"ReginaKay","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"184.151.222.153","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79237,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":1433461340,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"df34cf24f76be46b199c2fec8f0b846b","RawContent":"[quote name=\"ashlynm88\" post=\"1897752\" timestamp=\"1433269230\"]\nWe just got back from a wedding at Now Larimar in Punta Cana (which is also where I got engaged :) and would probably look into those more if we didn&#039;t want to try and get a different feel from a resort (not the same restaurants)...but the Dreams resorts seemed easy and maybe that is just because those are the ones that had been recommended to me at first. We are probably looking at around 60-80 guests (maybe, that&#039;s just a guess right now).\nFor some reason I thought Moon Palace may be more out of the price range I was shooting for for my guests, but TA Wendy suggested that one as a possibility as well, so I may have to look further into that one. I&#039;m just concerned with it&#039;s size.\nI&#039;m really wanting a great beach (not too rocky, or at least has a walkable\/swimable area) and I keep reading mix reviews on the \"types\" of beaches in the different resort locations.\nI spent all night last night reading all of @[member=\"calgarybride2015\"] posts\/boards. She did an amazing job! And I really liked how she was able to do the \"free\" package and add on the upgrades and have the private dinner in the palapa. I did read that there are no \"free\" safes in the rooms, which I find very odd. Any info on that? I am definitely going to spend some more time researching Grand Sirenis this evening. I did see it was kind of far from the airport as well like Dreams Tulum, but I also think I should try and concentrate more on what I am looking for in location and the wedding all while making sure I keep their travel in budget too no matter the trip to and from the airport. That is just one of the things that I have had in the back of my mind the last few days in researching.\nThanks for you input! It is greatly appreciated![\/quote]The safes was odd but I think it depends on your airline. Not all had a cost as I heard from Canada, Air Transat they were included. Otherwise I had minimal complaints. Also from Cancun it was about an hour on the bus. Any questions please feel free to ask! \n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk","Attachments":[],"Id":1897945,"PostDate":1433461239,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>ashlynm88, on 02 June 2015 - 02:20 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'><p>\nWe just got back from a wedding at Now Larimar in Punta Cana (which is also where I got engaged <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> and would probably look into those more if we didn't want to try and get a different feel from a resort (not the same restaurants)...but the Dreams resorts seemed easy and maybe that is just because those are the ones that had been recommended to me at first. We are probably looking at around 60-80 guests (maybe, that's just a guess right now).<br>\nFor some reason I thought Moon Palace may be more out of the price range I was shooting for for my guests, but TA Wendy suggested that one as a possibility as well, so I may have to look further into that one. I'm just concerned with it's size.<br>\nI'm really wanting a great beach (not too rocky, or at least has a walkable\/swimable area) and I keep reading mix reviews on the \"types\" of beaches in the different resort locations.<br>\nI spent all night last night reading all of @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"277873\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/277873-calgarybride2015\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">calgarybride2015<\/span><\/a> posts\/boards. She did an amazing job! And I really liked how she was able to do the \"free\" package and add on the upgrades and have the private dinner in the palapa. I did read that there are no \"free\" safes in the rooms, which I find very odd. Any info on that? I am definitely going to spend some more time researching Grand Sirenis this evening. I did see it was kind of far from the airport as well like Dreams Tulum, but I also think I should try and concentrate more on what I am looking for in location and the wedding all while making sure I keep their travel in budget too no matter the trip to and from the airport. That is just one of the things that I have had in the back of my mind the last few days in researching.<br>\nThanks for you input! It is greatly appreciated!<\/p><\/div><\/div>The safes was odd but I think it depends on your airline. Not all had a cost as I heard from Canada, Air Transat they were included. Otherwise I had minimal complaints. Also from Cancun it was about an hour on the bus. Any questions please feel free to ask! <br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>-Kim<\/p>\n<p>Married on 2015\/01\/21 at the Grand Sirenis Riviera Maya with 43 guests in attendance \u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Planning Thread -\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Pictures\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Review\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"kdeakin@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"68.145.235.0","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1399414202,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277873.jpg?_r=1422218225","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"calgarybride2015","Id":277873,"Name":"calgarybride2015","IsOnline":true}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":9,"TotalPages":1,"CurrentPage":0,"NextPage":-1,"PreviousPage":-1,"LastPage":0},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":1,"Type":"int"}]}
